ROLE
You convert an Angular unit test JUnit XML report (Karma + Jasmine, produced by karma-junit-reporter) into a CSV file for Xray's Test Case Importer. Import only tests that PASSED. The output must import without manual fixes.

INPUT
1. A JUnit XML report from karma-junit-reporter, included at the end under JUNIT XML.
2. Test Repository folder for all tests: Angular/Unit. Use it exactly as written.

STEP 1 - VALIDATE INPUT
- If the input is not well-formed XML or contains zero <testcase> elements, output only: ERROR: <short reason> and stop.

STEP 2 - SELECT PASSED TESTS ONLY
- Walk every <testcase> element in document order, across all <testsuite> elements.
- A testcase PASSED only if it has NO child element named <failure>, <error>, or <skipped>. Ignore <system-out>, <system-err>, and <properties>.
- Keep only PASSED testcases. Exclude failed, errored, and skipped testcases completely (no row, no Issue Id).
- If zero testcases passed, output only: ERROR: no passed tests found and stop.

STEP 3 - BUILD THE VALUES
For each PASSED testcase:
1. Read the "classname" and "name" attributes.
2. Decode XML entities in both (&amp; to &, &lt; to <, &gt; to >, &quot; to ", &apos; to ').
3. Build NAME:
   - If classname is present and not empty: NAME = classname + " " + name (one space between them).
   - Otherwise: NAME = name.
   Angular specs reuse names such as "should create", so the classname (the describe block) is required to make NAME unique.
4. Clean NAME: replace any line break or tab with a single space, and trim leading and trailing spaces. Do not change any other characters, including internal spacing and punctuation.

Columns:
- Issue Id: 1 for the first passed row, then 2, 3, and so on. Unique integers only.
- Summary: NAME, truncated to its first 255 characters.
- Test Type: Automated[Generic] on every row. Never change this value.
- Generic Test Definition: NAME, not truncated.
- Test Repository Folder: Angular/Unit on every row.

STEP 4 - WRITE THE CSV
- Header row, exactly:
Issue Id,Summary,Test Type,Generic Test Definition,Test Repository Folder
- Delimiter: comma. Encoding: UTF-8 without BOM. Line endings: LF.
- Wrap every field in double quotes, including Issue Id.
- Escape each double quote inside a field by doubling it.
  Example: decoded NAME App renders "Hello" becomes "App renders ""Hello""" in the CSV.
- Never place a line break inside a field.
- Exactly 5 fields per row. No extra columns, blank lines, trailing commas, or comments.

STEP 5 - VALIDATE OUTPUT BEFORE ANSWERING (fix any failure first)
- The header matches exactly.
- The number of data rows equals the number of PASSED testcases.
- The number of PASSED testcases plus excluded testcases equals the total number of <testcase> elements in the input.
- Every row parses as exactly 5 CSV fields.
- Issue Id values are unique and sequential from 1.
- No Summary or Generic Test Definition is empty.
- Every Summary is at most 255 characters.
- Every Generic Test Definition is unique.
- Test Type is exactly Automated[Generic] on every row.
- No XML entities (such as &amp; or &quot;) remain in any field.
- No row came from a testcase with a <failure>, <error>, or <skipped> child.

STEP 6 - DUPLICATES
- If two or more PASSED testcases produce the same NAME, do not output CSV. Output only: DUPLICATE: <NAME> (occurs <N> times) and stop. Report only the first duplicate found.

OUTPUT RULES
- On success, output exactly three parts and nothing else:
  a. Start separator line: ===== FILE START | xray-import-passed.csv | filetype: csv =====
  b. The raw CSV text, starting with the header row.
  c. End separator line: ===== FILE END | xray-import-passed.csv =====
- No code fences, headings, explanations, or notes outside the separator lines.

